# Liquid URLs

Every internal href, src, and CSS url must go through `| relative_url` or `| absolute_url`. Never hardcode `/site`. Local `baseurl` is empty; prod `baseurl` is `/site`. The filter is what prefixes correctly.

Canonical and share URLs: `{{ site.url }}{{ site.baseurl }}{{ page.url }}` (already in `_includes/head.html`).

Nested pages (`about-me/`, `blog/`, `portfolio/<slug>/`) break if assets use `../public/...`. Root-absolute Liquid paths are depth-safe.

```html
<!-- BAD: hardcoded /site; nested ../public breaks on about-me/, blog/, portfolio/ -->
<link href="/site/public/css/styles.css" />
<img src="../../public/uploads/2024/03/hero.jpg" />

<!-- GOOD -->
<link href="{{ '/public/css/styles.css' | relative_url }}" />
<img src="{{ '/public/uploads/2024/03/hero.jpg' | relative_url }}" />
```

`_includes/top-banner.html` still uses a nested `../../../../public/...` background. New code must not copy that pattern; use `relative_url`.
